      "html": "<div class=\"ds-modal\"><h2 class=\"ds-modal-title\">Demo access</h2><p class=\"ds-modal-copy\">Any email creates a local session.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-modal{max-width:560px;padding:20px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:0;background:var(--bg-canvas);color:var(--copy);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px}.ds-modal-title{margin:0 0 12px;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:28px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:400;color:var(--text)}.ds-modal-copy{margin:0;line-height:1.55}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Cutoff Ledger",
    "overview": [
      "A printed JoSAA cutoff almanac crossed with a terminal. The page is a ledger that finds your line in it. It is not a dashboard of recommendation cards: no centered hero card, no card grid, no rounded shadows. Density is honest. A student under counselling pressure should scan a ruled table and find their rank in it faster than any chat UI would let them.",
      "The world runs dark only. A deep ink navy ground, parchment text, terracotta and sage and sunkiss state ticks, tidal blue actions, 1px hairlines, and square corners everywhere. Source Serif 4 speaks in display sizes, Commit Mono carries everything operational, Departure Mono marks folios and axis labels. The signature element is the Rank Rail: a log-scale rail with the student rank fixed at center and each closing rank ticked left for reach or right for safe."
    ],
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark only, deep ink ground, no light theme and no theme toggle.",
      "Square corners everywhere. No border radius survives.",
      "1px hairlines separate everything. No drop shadows at rest.",
      "Serif for display, mono for everything operational.",
      "Numbers are tabular and right-aligned in data columns.",
      "Uppercase micro labels with 0.08em tracking, never a kicker above a heading.",
      "Accent blue is rare: primary actions and the active step only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Tidal blue marks actions and the current step, nothing else. Data states speak in terracotta, sunkiss, and sage, not blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No New Hex Rule",
        "body": "Every color in the UI resolves to a token in tokens.css. Screens add no hex values of their own.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Serif Statement Rule",
        "body": "Serif appears in display sizes, headlines, institute names and the rank input only. If a piece of text is operational, it is mono.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Kicker Rule",
        "body": "Never an eyebrow or running head above a heading. The heading carries its own weight.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-By-Default Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces are flat. No shadows anywhere; depth is tonal layering plus hairlines. Focus rings are the only raised element.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep every screen dark. Deep Ink ground, no light variant, no toggle.",
      "Do resolve every color from tokens.css. No new hex values in screen CSS.",
      "Do use tabular numerals for every number that can change or be compared.",
      "Do let hairlines do the separating. Rows, sections, toolbars: 1px rules.",
      "Do keep serif for the one display statement per screen and institute names.",
      "Do label missing data as a plain dash, never \"N/A\".",
      "Do keep the accent blue rare: primary actions, active step, focus."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use border radius anywhere. The system is square.",
      "Don't add shadows, glows, or blurred backdrops.",
      "Don't put a kicker or eyebrow above a heading.",
      "Don't build card grids of equal tiles. The results screen is a ruled table.",
      "Don't use color alone to carry meaning. State ticks also carry text labels.",
      "Don't round inputs or buttons just a little. 0 means 0."
    ]
  }
}